<div class="section-label jump-target" id="current-status">Current Status</div>
<h2>What Is Known Now</h2>

<p>The SR-177 Weber County extension segment from 1800 North to 4000 South is in the State Environmental Study phase.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} UDOT published the Draft State Environmental Study on November 6, 2026. It identifies a Preferred Alternative: a four-lane freeway along 5100 West from 1800 North to 4000 South, with diamond interchanges at 1800 North and 5500 South and a single-point urban interchange at 4000 South.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} Volume 2 of the draft maps the proposed right-of-way.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol2-nov2026" %} These are drafts: UDOT is taking comments through December 11, 2026, and says the Final State Environmental Study is expected in early 2027.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</p>

<div class="callout info">
  <p><strong>Draft, not final:</strong> UDOT says property impacts "may be refined during the final design and right-of-way acquisition phases."{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} UDOT carried forward a "hybrid" alignment: west of 5100 West in the south, crossing to the east side north of the 5500 South interchange.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-appendix-nov2026" %} The "Hybrid Concept Design" layers seen in public ArcGIS working maps in May 2026 appear to show that concept; the draft study's maps are the controlling source.{% cite "arcgis-sr177-project-layers-may2026" %}{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol2-nov2026" %}</p>
</div>

