<div class="task-grid">
  <div class="task-card">
    <div class="task-label">Study phase</div>
    <h3>Draft study open for comment</h3>
    <p>UDOT published the Draft State Environmental Study on November 6, 2026. Comments are due December 11, 2026; the Final State Environmental Study is expected in early 2027.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="task-card">
    <div class="task-label">Funding</div>
    <h3>Construction unfunded</h3>
    <p>The regional plan lists this segment in Phase 2 (2033–2042), an assumed-funding window, not a commitment. UDOT's draft 2027–2032 program includes no construction money for it, and the draft study says it could be built in two phases "as funding becomes available."{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-draft-stip-2027-2032" %}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="task-card">
    <div class="task-label">Alignment</div>
    <h3>Draft Preferred Alternative</h3>
    <p>A four-lane freeway along 5100 West with interchanges at 1800 North, 5500 South, and 4000 South. It is a draft until UDOT approves the Final State Environmental Study.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section-label jump-target" id="decision-points">Decision Points</div>
<h2>Where the Timeline Becomes Actionable</h2>

<p>The Draft State Environmental Study, published November 6, 2026, provides the first formal alignment maps for the Weber County segment.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol2-nov2026" %} The formal comment period runs through December 11, 2026.{% cite "udot-ses-public-hearing-nov2026" %}</p>

<ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 1.8;">
  <li><strong>How to comment:</strong> by December 11, 2026, by email to sr177extension@utah.gov, through the online comment form linked from the study page, by mail to the SR-177 Study Team, 1265 E Fort Union Blvd, Suite 200, Cottonwood Heights, UT 84047, or in person at the hearing.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Online informational presentation:</strong> held Monday, November 9, 2026. UDOT says the recording and hearing materials will be posted on the study page beginning November 11.{% cite "udot-ses-online-presentation-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Official in-person public hearing:</strong> set for Tuesday, November 10, 2026, 4:30–7:30 p.m., at Roy Junior High School, 5347 South 2100 West, Roy. It is an open house with no formal presentation; right-of-way specialists are scheduled to answer property-specific questions.{% cite "udot-ses-public-hearing-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Neighborhood meetings:</strong> invitation-only meetings for property owners and tenants affected by planned impacts were held in early November 2026.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Final State Environmental Study:</strong> UDOT says it is expected to be published in early 2027 and will include responses to comments.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</li>
</ul>

<p>West Haven City Council was told on July 15, 2026 that UDOT was moving toward completing the study before November 2026;{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes-jul2026" %} the draft was published on November 6.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</p>

